{"quarters":{"2026-06-30":{"end":"2026-06-30","label":"Q2 2026","fq":2,"fy":2026,"cal":"CY2026Q2","form":"10-Q","accn":"0001628280-26-054571","filed":"2026-08-07","doc_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1849056/000162828026054571/oklo-20260630.htm","index_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1849056/000162828026054571/0001628280-26-054571-index.htm","raw":{"revenue":1210000,"cor":null,"gp":null,"rd":39474000,"sm":null,"ga":34205000,"sga":null,"costs_total":null,"opex_total":74400000,"oi":-73190000,"pretax":-51689000,"tax":-3153000,"ni":-48536000,"pl":null,"nci":null,"ocf":-47592000,"da":337000,"dep":null,"amort":97000,"sbc":14358000,"rev_contract":1210000,"capex":94091000},"q1_end":"2026-03-31","py_end":"2025-06-30","raw_q1":{"revenue":null,"cor":null,"gp":null,"rd":27049000,"sm":null,"ga":24200000,"sga":null,"costs_total":null,"opex_total":51249000,"oi":-51249000,"pretax":-29910000,"tax":3155000,"ni":-33065000,"pl":null,"nci":null,"ocf":-17867000,"da":163000,"dep":null,"amort":null,"sbc":15586000,"rev_contract":null,"capex":32810000},"raw_py":{"revenue":0,"cor":null,"gp":null,"rd":11468000,"sm":null,"ga":16547000,"sga":null,"costs_total":null,"opex_total":28015000,"oi":-28015000,"pretax":-24254000,"tax":431000,"ni":-24685000,"pl":null,"nci":null,"ocf":-18471000,"da":125000,"dep":null,"amort":0,"sbc":11365000,"rev_contract":0,"capex":877000},"lines_struct":null,"lines":null,"lines_py":null,"notes":{"cor":[{"heading":"Cost of Sales","text":"Cost of sales includes direct costs incurred in satisfying performance obligations under customer contracts."}],"opex":[{"heading":"Operating Expenses","text":"Operating expenses consist of research and development and general and administrative expenses."}],"costs":[{"heading":"Operating Expenses","text":"Operating expenses consist of research and development and general and administrative expenses."}],"rd":[{"heading":"Research and Development","text":"Research and development (\u201cR&D\u201d) expenses represent costs incurred to develop our technologies. These costs consist of personnel costs, including salaries, employee benefit costs, bonuses, and stock-based compensation expenses, software costs, computing costs, hardware and experimental supplies, and expenses for outside engineering contractors for analytical work and consulting costs. We expense all R&D costs in the periods in which they are incurred; however, occasionally, reimbursements could be received in a subsequent period.\n\nWe have several recycling technology projects awarded as R&D cost-share projects (the \u201ccost-share projects\u201d) through the DOE\u2019s Advanced Research Projects Agency \u2013 Energy (\u201cARPA-E\u201d) and the DOE Technology Commercialization Fund (\u201cTCF\u201d). The ARPA-E and TCF projects involve cost-sharing of project costs as well as reimbursement of certain"}],"ga":[{"heading":"General and Administrative","text":"General and administrative (\u201cG&A\u201d) expenses primarily comprise various components not related to R&D, such as personnel costs, regulatory fees, promotion expenses, costs associated with maintaining and filing intellectual property, meals and entertainment expenses, travel expenses, and other expenditures related to external professional services including legal, engineering, marketing, human resources, procurement, audit, finance, and accounting services. Personnel costs include salaries, benefits, and stock-based compensation expenses. As we continue to grow and expand our workforce and operations, and in light of the increased costs associated with operating as a public company, we anticipate that our G&A expenses will rise for the foreseeable future."}],"nonop":[{"heading":"Other Income","text":"Other income consists of interest and dividend income on our portfolio of marketable debt securities."}],"tax":[{"heading":"Income Taxes","text":"Income taxes consist of income taxes in jurisdictions in which we conduct business. We have a full valuation allowance for deferred tax assets, including net operating loss carryforwards and tax credits related primarily to R&D. Federal and state income taxes may be incurred as a result of our revenue and interest income from investments, after available tax deductions and tax attribute carry-overs."}],"ocf":[{"heading":"Operating Activities","text":"Net cash used in operating activities was $65.5 million in 2026, compared to $30.7 million in 2025. The $34.8 million increase in net cash used in operating activities from 2025 to 2026 was primarily driven by operating expenses as we continue to scale our operations, consisting of $37.8 million cash used for payroll and employee benefits of personnel and $74.9 million in other costs, primarily consisting of professional services for consulting on research and development activities, and legal and accounting fees on general and administrative activities. These increases were partially offset by $45.4 million in higher cash interest and dividend income, resulting from our increased balance of cash, cash equivalents and marketable debt securities."}],"capex":[{"heading":null,"text":"We expect our total cash used in operating activities for 2026 to be in the range of $120 million to $150 million and our total cash used for purchases of property, plant and equipment to be in the range of $400 million to $500 million."}],"net sales":[{"heading":"Revenue","text":"In June 2026, we completed the acquisitions of two advanced engineering companies, ARMEC, LLC and Creative Engineers, Inc. These two highly specialized teams bring precision manufacturing and mechanical engineering expertise specializing in high-precision machining and prototyping, and mechanical engineering services and chemical process engineering expertise in sodium and alkali-metal systems, both for the nuclear industry, to expand Oklo's engineering capabilities. Both of these newly acquired subsidiaries continue to provide engineering services to an established group of customers. Revenue is generated from contracts with government agencies and commercial counterparties for engineering, design, licensing support, technical consulting, research and development activities, and other services related to advanced nuclear technology development."}]},"capex_src":{"concept":"us-gaap:PaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment","label":"Purchases of property, plant and equipment","how":"xbrl"},"src":{"revenue":{"c":"us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax","l":"Revenue from Contract with Customer, Excluding Assessed Tax","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"rd":{"c":"us-gaap:ResearchAndDevelopmentExpense","l":"Research and development","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"ga":{"c":"us-gaap:GeneralAndAdministrativeExpense","l":"General and administrative","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"opex_total":{"c":"us-gaap:OperatingExpenses","l":"Operating Expenses","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"oi":{"c":"us-gaap:OperatingIncomeLoss","l":"Operating loss","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"pretax":{"c":"us-gaap:IncomeLossFromContinuingOperationsBeforeIncomeTaxesExtraordinaryItemsNoncontrollingInterest","l":"Income (Loss) from Continuing Operations before Income Taxes, Noncontrolling Interest","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"tax":{"c":"us-gaap:IncomeTaxExpenseBenefit","l":"Income tax benefit (expense)","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"ni":{"c":"us-gaap:NetIncomeLoss","l":"Net loss","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"ocf":{"c":"us-gaap:NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities","l":"Net cash used in operating activities","ytd":true,"how":"xbrl"},"da":{"c":"us-gaap:DepreciationDepletionAndAmortization","l":"Depreciation, Depletion and Amortization","ytd":true,"how":"xbrl"},"amort":{"c":"us-gaap:AmortizationOfIntangibleAssets","l":"Amortization of Intangible Assets","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"sbc":{"c":"us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensation","l":"Share-based Payment Arrangement, Noncash Expense","ytd":true,"how":"xbrl"},"rev_contract":{"c":"us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax","l":"Revenue from Contract with Customer, Excluding Assessed Tax","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"capex":{"c":"us-gaap:PaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment","l":"Purchases of property, plant and equipment","ytd":true,"how":"xbrl"}},"co_fcf":null,"co_status":"no_release","co_errors":0,"co_tried":1}},"dims_ytd":{"2026-06-30":{}},"profile":{"cik":1849056,"name":"Oklo Inc.","tickers":["OKLO"],"exchanges":["NYSE"],"sic":"4911","industry":"Electric Services","sector":"utilities","fye":"1231","state":"DE","category":"<br>Emerging growth company"},"periods":{"q":["2025-06-30","2026-06-30"],"fy":[]},"intro":{"text":"We founded Oklo in 2013 with the goal of revolutionizing the energy landscape by developing clean, reliable, affordable energy solutions at scale. According to the International Energy Agency, global electricity production is expected to increase over 75% by 2050 driven by electrification of buildings, transportation, and industry; increased use of air conditioning in the developing world; and increased consumption from data centers and cloud services. Our business addresses this demand by producing electricity and heat from our Aurora powerhouses which can run on fresh, recycled, or down-blended nuclear fuel. We are also commercializing nuclear fuel recycling technology that can convert used nuclear fuel into usable fuel for our powerhouses and those of others.","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1849056/000162828026018698/oklo-20251231.htm","filed":"2026-03-17","source":"10-K"},"keep":7,"hist":2,"da_v":2,"quality":{"v":6,"unit":"USD","q":[{"end":"2024-09-30","start":"2024-06-30","label":"Q3 2024","ni":-9960000,"basis":"ni","ocf":-7879000,"assets_open":299185613,"assets_close":293793833,"wc":{"rev":null,"cor":null,"days":92,"ar_o":null,"ar_c":null,"inv_o":null,"inv_c":null,"ap_o":1068205,"ap_c":361240,"ap_proxy":false,"has_inv":false,"dso":null,"dio":null,"dpo":null,"ccc":null},"bridge":{"start":-9960000,"basis":"ni","items":[["da",68000,[4,